WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.548
We had made many improvements to our homes at Falconhurst and Tentholm.

2
00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:09.143
But there was one more improvement that my wife wanted us to make at Falconhurst.

3
00:00:09.144 --> 00:00:13.070
"I think that our nest in the tree is perfect," she said.

4
00:00:13.071 --> 00:00:17.387
"But I'd like to be able to reach it without climbing that dreadful ladder.

5
00:00:17.388 --> 00:00:19.744
Can you build a flight of steps?"

6
00:00:19.745 --> 00:00:24.540
"We might be able to build a staircase inside the trunk of the tree," I replied.

7
00:00:24.541 --> 00:00:27.387
"I've often suspected that the trunk is hollow.

8
00:00:27.388 --> 00:00:31.484
Didn't you say that you've noticed bees coming from a hole in the tree?"

9
00:00:31.485 --> 00:00:35.088
Before my wife could reply, little Franz piped up.

10
00:00:35.089 --> 00:00:39.540
"Oh yes! I went to look at them, and one stung me.

11
00:00:39.541 --> 00:00:42.703
I almost cried but I didn't."

12
00:00:42.704 --> 00:00:48.083
"Brave boy!" I said. "Let's see if the tree is really hollow."

13
00:00:48.084 --> 00:00:51.471
Led by Jack, the boys were soon peeping into the hole.

14
00:00:51.472 --> 00:00:54.298
They tapped the tree to see if it sounded hollow.

15
00:00:54.299 --> 00:00:57.364
In their eagerness they forgot who lived in the tree.

16
00:00:57.365 --> 00:01:02.448
The bees, disturbed by all this activity, swarmed out and attacked the boys.

17
00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:05.626
"Ow! Ow! Ow!" cried Jack.

18
00:01:05.627 --> 00:01:09.843
"Nasty bees!" said Fritz as he tried to swat them away.

19
00:01:09.844 --> 00:01:13.779
My wife and I pulled the boys away from the angry bees.

20
00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.279
They had all been stung on their hands and faces.

21
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:23.034
Before we built a staircase, we removed the bees to a new nesting place in a large gourd.

22
00:01:23.035 --> 00:01:27.222
We made good use of the honey and wax that they left behind in the tree.

23
00:01:27.223 --> 00:01:29.799
Then we began working on the stairs.

24
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:33.590
At the base of the tree, we made an opening for a door.

25
00:01:33.591 --> 00:01:37.633
We attached a door we'd taken earlier from the captain's cabin.

26
00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:44.464
Next we cleared out the rotted wood from the center of the trunk and put up a stout sapling to provide a center pole.

27
00:01:44.465 --> 00:01:48.158
With planks from the wreck, we then fashioned steps.

28
00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:52.194
As we worked, we cut windows in the trunk for light and air.

29
00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:58.203
When we reached the top of the center pole, we added another sapling to reach the floor of our home above.

30
00:01:58.204 --> 00:02:00.623
We even included two handrails!

31
00:02:00.624 --> 00:02:06.958
This task took us a whole month, during which we also had to care for our animals.

32
00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:10.636
By now several of the goats and sheep had produced offspring.

33
00:02:10.637 --> 00:02:15.636
To keep these frisky youngsters from straying, we tied bells around their necks.

34
00:02:15.637 --> 00:02:18.423
Juno produced a fine litter of puppies.

35
00:02:18.424 --> 00:02:25.746
Jack introduced his little jackal, Fangs, to the litter, and, to his delight, Juno adopted the wild dog.

36
00:02:25.747 --> 00:02:29.298
The other pets were also flourishing and learning new tasks.

37
00:02:29.299 --> 00:02:36.544
After giving us much trouble, Storm, the buffalo, was now capable of carrying both people and things.

38
00:02:36.545 --> 00:02:42.858
Fritz was so busy teaching his eagle, Pounce, to hunt live prey that he gave Knips to Ernest.

39
00:02:42.859 --> 00:02:48.835
Knips was not allowed to remain idle, as Ernest decided that he should be taught to do something useful.

40
00:02:48.836 --> 00:02:52.589
He and Jack made a small basket that fit on the monkey's back.

41
00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:58.839
Then Ernest taught Knips to climb coconut and other tall trees and to bring down the fruit in the basket.

42
00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:06.507
Jack tried to teach Fangs to retrieve, but the jackal kept eating everything it caught.

43
00:03:06.508 --> 00:03:11.836
Meanwhile I was determined to have some waterproof boots before the start of the rainy season.

44
00:03:11.837 --> 00:03:17.531
To make a mold, I filled a pair of socks with sand and coated them with a thin layer of clay.

45
00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:20.261
Then I brushed on several layers of rubber.

46
00:03:20.262 --> 00:03:26.007
When that had dried, I broke the mold and added some buffalo-hide soles.

47
00:03:26.008 --> 00:03:29.836
"These are wonderful!" said Fritz as he tried on my boots.

48
00:03:29.837 --> 00:03:31.687
"Can you make me a pair?"

49
00:03:31.688 --> 00:03:34.887
"Me too!" cried all the other boys.

50
00:03:34.888 --> 00:03:42.361
I was delighted to fill their orders, and soon everyone in the family had a pair of comfortable, durable waterproof boots.

51
00:03:42.362 --> 00:03:47.870
The boys had long been complaining about having to walk to the stream and bring back heavy buckets of water.

52
00:03:47.871 --> 00:03:53.717
So our next job was to build a dam with a series of pipes to carry the water to Falconhurst.

53
00:03:53.718 --> 00:04:00.911
One day, as we were finishing this task, we were startled by the roaring or bellowing of a wild beast.

54
00:04:00.912 --> 00:04:04.969
The sound was so strange that I couldn't imagine what animal had made it.

55
00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.651
"Perhaps it's a lion," offered Jack.

56
00:04:07.652 --> 00:04:10.188
"No, a gorilla," said Fritz.

57
00:04:10.189 --> 00:04:13.231
"More likely a hyena," said Ernest.

58
00:04:13.232 --> 00:04:17.354
"Whatever it is," I said, "we must be ready when it arrives.

59
00:04:17.355 --> 00:04:21.179
All of you, hurry to the nest while I secure the door."

60
00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:26.574
I left the dogs outside to protect our animals, closed the door, and joined my family.

61
00:04:26.575 --> 00:04:30.993
Every eye was on watch. Every gun was loaded.

62
00:04:30.994 --> 00:04:36.825
The dreadful sound came nearer.

